    "The purpose of a Miniature Circuit Breaker (MCB) is to protect electrical wiring by preventing overheating and potential electrical fires caused by continuous overload or short circuits.",
    "The MCB functions through two mechanisms.",
    "Thermal Overload Protection uses a bimetallic strip that bends when excess current generates heat.",
    "If the current exceeds safe levels for a certain time (10 to 60 seconds), the bent strip trips the circuit open.",
    "This stops the current flow before the wire's insulation can melt.",
    "Magnetic Short-Circuit Protection activates when a high fault current surges.",
    "A high fault current can happen if a live wire touches a neutral wire.",
    "An electromagnetic solenoid creates a magnetic field that quickly drives a plunger to open the circuit in less than 10 milliseconds.",
    "Opening the circuit extinguishes any electrical arc to prevent ignition of fires.",
    "The MCB safeguards copper wires from damage.",
    "The MCB helps to prevent electrical fires.",
    "The MCB does not provide protection against electric shock."
] 

